{"When result_processor raises an exception, the worker logs the error but still runs the finally block and marks the offset complete, causing transient processing failures to be skipped instead of retried": 0.8945673704147339, "Broad exception path completes the offset for any decode, grouping, or queue submission failure, making messages committable without the result processor ever running": 0.930110514163971, "shutdown() sets each worker's stop flag before the queues are drained, causing workers to exit early and leave queued items unprocessed": 0.8725179433822632, "close() stops the commit thread before shutting down the worker pool, so offsets completed while workers finish have no later commit pass and already-processed messages can be redelivered": 0.9528550505638123, "Factory creates one FixedQueuePool but each SimpleQueueProcessingStrategy.close() shuts that pool down, so if the same factory instance creates another strategy after close or rebalance, submissions target queues whose workers are already stopped": 0.8984827399253845}